Chrome allows you to load unpacked local directories as extensions, you can build a lightweight, custom Extension in under two minutes. This gives you total control: it keeps Google as your default address bar search engine, but completely strips the New Tab page of Doodles, animations, and clutter.

Here is how to load your own local "Doodle Blocker" extension.

Open Chrome and navigate to chrome://extensions/ in the address bar.

In the top-right corner of the Extensions page, toggle the Developer mode switch to ON.

In the top-left corner, click the Load unpacked button.

Select the custom-new-tab folder you created.
